1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,652
Fourteenth of March, 2024. A small town in
Serbia.

2
00:00:06,782 --> 00:00:09,953
Three hundred and seventy people in the
stands.

3
00:00:10,083 --> 00:00:13,015
And Olympiacos, three goals down.

4
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:18,746
By midnight, it was the biggest away win
in the club’s whole European history.

5
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:23,571
Bill Shankly said football was more
important than life and death.

6
00:00:23,701 --> 00:00:28,658
Ten thousand supporters in eighty
countries voted it the greatest thing ever

7
00:00:28,698 --> 00:00:30,170
said about the game.

8
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:33,657
In Piraeus, nobody needs that explained.

9
00:00:33,787 --> 00:00:37,009
They call this club Thrylos. The Legend.

10
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:40,966
But one week earlier, the Legend was dead
and buried.

11
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:46,663
Round of sixteen, first leg. The
Karaiskakis.

12
00:00:46,793 --> 00:00:50,131
31,054 inside.

13
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,815
Six wins in a row since José Luis
Mendilibar arrived in February.

14
00:00:55,945 --> 00:01:01,849
And Maccabi Tel Aviv? The last time, in
2010, they had knocked

15
00:01:01,889 --> 00:01:05,654
Olympiacos out on away goals. Unfinished
business.

16
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:09,912
Mendilibar had been the manager for
twenty-five days.

17
00:01:10,042 --> 00:01:14,595
A Thursday night in Piraeus, and the whole
ground expected a win.

18
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:18,043
Nine minutes in, it was two-nil to
Maccabi.

19
00:01:18,173 --> 00:01:21,571
Eran Zahavi. Ido Shahar.

20
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:26,246
El Kaabi pulled one back. Then Zahavi
again.

21
00:01:26,376 --> 00:01:28,036
Then Dor Peretz.

22
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:34,162
One-three at half-time. A full Karaiskakis,
and you could hear the Maccabi

23
00:01:34,202 --> 00:01:34,582
bench.

24
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:40,448
One-four. At home. The heaviest home
defeat Olympiacos have ever

25
00:01:40,488 --> 00:01:42,745
suffered in this competition.

26
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,496
Mendilibar did not hide.

27
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:49,639
On the other bench, Robbie Keane chose his
words carefully.

28
00:01:49,769 --> 00:01:50,969
Remember them.

29
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,467
In Israel, the morning papers were a
party.

30
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:59,654
Maccabi Tel Aviv jumps out to big lead
over Olympiacos.

31
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:02,450
Three days later, it got worse.

32
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:06,765
The derby. Panathinaikos, at the
Karaiskakis.

33
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:11,652
Two home defeats in one week, one of them
to the eternal enemy.

34
00:02:11,782 --> 00:02:16,727
If football is a religion, this was the
week people stopped going to church.

35
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:21,714
A word from the stands. These films are
made for people who still keep the

36
00:02:21,754 --> 00:02:25,901
ticket stub in a drawer. If that's you,
hit subscribe.

37
00:02:26,031 --> 00:02:28,593
There is always room in the away end.

38
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:35,051
The second leg was Maccabi’s home game,
but it could not be played in Israel.

39
00:02:35,181 --> 00:02:41,083
Because of the war, it went to Serbia,
behind closed doors, at the TSC

40
00:02:41,123 --> 00:02:42,280
Arena in Bačka Topola.

41
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:45,291
Three hundred and seventy people.

42
00:02:45,421 --> 00:02:49,861
And it was José Luis Mendilibar’s
sixty-third birthday.

43
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:52,967
Maccabi had won their last five.

44
00:02:53,097 --> 00:02:58,027
They were ninety minutes from the first
European quarter-final in their history.

45
00:02:58,157 --> 00:03:01,380
All they had to do was not lose by three.

46
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:06,026
Back in Piraeus, a whole city sat down in
front of a screen.

47
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:11,385
Ten minutes. Daniel Podence. Four-two on
aggregate.

48
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:15,641
Thirty-six. The captain, Kostas Fortounis.

49
00:03:15,771 --> 00:03:16,905
Four-three.

50
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:21,910
First-half stoppage time. Ayoub El Kaabi,
with his head.

51
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,149
Four-four.

52
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:26,385
Then Zahavi, from the penalty spot.

53
00:03:26,515 --> 00:03:28,830
Five-four Maccabi, again.

54
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:34,312
Sixty-five. El Kaabi again. Four-one on
the night.

55
00:03:34,442 --> 00:03:37,926
The exact score of Piraeus, turned upside
down.

56
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:41,569
Five each on aggregate after ninety
minutes.

57
00:03:41,699 --> 00:03:42,979
Extra time.

58
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:49,289
Ninety-three. Stevan Jovetić, his first
goal in European competition

59
00:03:49,329 --> 00:03:50,535
for fourteen years.

60
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:56,827
A hundred and three. Youssef El-Arabi, who
had only come on in the eighty-eighth

61
00:03:56,867 --> 00:03:58,545
minute. Six-one.

62
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:03,722
Seven goals to five. From three down to
the quarter-finals.

63
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:09,230
Robbie Keane, a week after halftime, had
one line for the other dressing room.

64
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:16,669
Proto Thema, in Athens, wrote that no team
in

65
00:04:16,709 --> 00:04:18,988
European cup history had ever turned round
a three-goal home defeat.

66
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:23,880
Conference League: Maccabi Tel Aviv,
Olympiacos, one-six.

67
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:27,354
In Ireland, they wrote about the other
side of it.

68
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:32,644
Eran Zahavi had scored three of Maccabi’s
five goals in the tie.

69
00:04:32,774 --> 00:04:34,115
He said it best.

70
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:39,795
And Mendilibar? He said they had never
even talked about going through.

71
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:45,493
Only about a good night. Then the second
goal went in, and the third, and he

72
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:47,497
said they were filled with confidence.

73
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:52,284
When the team landed in Athens, the
supporters were there to meet them.

74
00:04:52,414 --> 00:04:56,556
Scenes of madness, the Spanish agency EFE
called it.

75
00:04:56,940 --> 00:05:01,393
Two months later, an English paper went
looking for the great comebacks.

76
00:05:01,523 --> 00:05:06,981
Only three times in UEFA’s three competitions
had a team lost at home by two

77
00:05:07,021 --> 00:05:09,151
goals or more and still gone through.

78
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:16,263
The Legend. A club with a laurel-crowned
youth on its badge, and a week in March

79
00:05:16,303 --> 00:05:18,460
it will never let anyone forget.

80
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:23,297
Before the final in May, Mendilibar looked
back at Bačka Topola.

81
00:05:23,427 --> 00:05:27,781
For sure, he said, that game showed
everyone what we are capable of.

82
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:33,471
Eleven weeks after that night, Olympiacos
won the Conference League in Athens.

83
00:05:33,601 --> 00:05:37,486
The first European trophy ever won by a
Greek club.

84
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:42,050
Piraeus. Bačka Topola. Athens.

85
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:46,076
Three hundred and seventy people saw it in
the ground.

86
00:05:46,206 --> 00:05:51,429
Every Olympiacos supporter will tell you
where they were when the sixth went in.

87
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:54,501
More important than life and death.

88
00:05:54,631 --> 00:06:00,098
Ask anyone in Piraeus about that week in
March, and they will tell you Shankly

89
00:06:00,138 --> 00:06:01,213
was being modest.

90
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:06,906
Every match in this film is waiting in the
FanLife archive, with the games, the

91
00:06:06,946 --> 00:06:09,509
trivia and the stories of the whole club.

92
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:13,611
Come and play it at fanlife.dubelteam.com.

93
00:06:13,741 --> 00:06:18,627
And if this story was yours too,
subscribe, and the next one will find you.
